(7699270, 1263332, 114285, '<td valign="top">I wonder whose photo this was. I really love the high ceilings. I never wouldve picked it as your home. I looked up the new area that you are living in, really cant complain, it still looks pretty beautiful. Is this where you have been, moving house? I thought maybe you had departed from Dpc.<br/> <br/></td>', 'I wonder whose photo this was. I really love the high ceilings. I never wouldve picked it as your home. I looked up the new area that you are living in, really cant complain, it still looks pretty beautiful. Is this where you have been, moving house? I thought maybe you had departed from Dpc. ', '2021-08-20 03:51:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7699273, 1263445, 114285, '<td valign="top">Oh to live in the countryside, one-day one-day. A very beautiful setting. This was always going to be the one to beat.</td>', 'Oh to live in the countryside, one-day one-day. A very beautiful setting. This was always going to be the one to beat.', '2021-08-20 03:52:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7699274, 1263420, 114285, '<td valign="top">I really love how you framed this image. You must have been receiving a lot of rain. very green over there.</td>', 'I really love how you framed this image. You must have been receiving a lot of rain. very green over there.', '2021-08-20 03:53:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(7699276, 1263443, 114285, '<td valign="top">Is this your new home area, looks like a beautiful little cul-de-sac, surrounded by trees, how lovely.</td>', 'Is this your new home area, looks like a beautiful little cul-de-sac, surrounded by trees, how lovely.', '2021-08-20 03:54:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(7699283, 1263332, 123833, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> I wonder whose photo this was. I really love the high ceilings. I never wouldve picked it as your home. I looked up the new area that you are living in, really cant complain, it still looks pretty beautiful. Is this where you have been, moving house? I thought maybe you had departed from Dpc. </i></td></tr></table> I did depart DPC with the intention to spend all spare time on 3D environments and forgetting photography for a while but one week after that we got horrible news that the owner of the house where we rented an apartment has terminal cancer with 3 to 6 months to live and will be selling the house, including our rental apartment. I did not do any 3D nor photography after that, there was a lot of stress and hassle. After 3 months our world is slowly getting to the new normal so I started with a bit of photography but I will be soon back to 3D. I won''t be entering many challenges, if any at all, after the current ones run out.</td>', 'Originally posted by Neat: I wonder whose photo this was. I really love the high ceilings. I never wouldve picked it as your home. I looked up the new area that you are living in, really cant complain, it still looks pretty beautiful. Is this where you have been, moving house? I thought maybe you had departed from Dpc.  I did depart DPC with the intention to spend all spare time on 3D environments and forgetting photography for a while but one week after that we got horrible news that the owner of the house where we rented an apartment has terminal cancer with 3 to 6 months to live and will be selling the house, including our rental apartment. I did not do any 3D nor photography after that, there was a lot of stress and hassle. After 3 months our world is slowly getting to the new normal so I started with a bit of photography but I will be soon back to 3D. I won''t be entering many challenges, if any at all, after the current ones run out.', '2021-08-20 08:08:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7699284, 1263332, 123833, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MargaretNet:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> I wonder whose photo this was. I really love the high ceilings. I never wouldve picked it as your home. I looked up the new area that you are living in, really cant complain, it still looks pretty beautiful. Is this where you have been, moving house? I thought maybe you had departed from Dpc. </i></td></tr></table> I did depart DPC with the intention to spend all spare time on 3D environments and forgetting photography for a while but one week after that we got horrible news that the owner of the house where we rented an apartment has terminal cancer with 3 to 6 months to live and will be selling the house, including our rental apartment. I did not do any 3D nor photography after that, there was a lot of stress and hassle. After 3 months our world is slowly getting to the new normal so I started with a bit of photography but I will be soon back to 3D. I won''t be entering many challenges, if any at all, after the current ones run out. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>PS I would enter some challenges if there was a new ruleset called NO RULES at all, anything goes. That would allow me to enter still frames from flying over my 3D worlds :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2021-08-20 07:12:49.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by MargaretNet: Originally posted by Neat: I wonder whose photo this was. I really love the high ceilings. I never wouldve picked it as your home. I looked up the new area that you are living in, really cant complain, it still looks pretty beautiful. Is this where you have been, moving house? I thought maybe you had departed from Dpc.  I did depart DPC with the intention to spend all spare time on 3D environments and forgetting photography for a while but one week after that we got horrible news that the owner of the house where we rented an apartment has terminal cancer with 3 to 6 months to live and will be selling the house, including our rental apartment. I did not do any 3D nor photography after that, there was a lot of stress and hassle. After 3 months our world is slowly getting to the new normal so I started with a bit of photography but I will be soon back to 3D. I won''t be entering many challenges, if any at all, after the current ones run out.  PS I would enter some challenges if there was a new ruleset called NO RULES at all, anything goes. That would allow me to enter still frames from flying over my 3D worlds :)', '2021-08-20 08:11:15.000000', '2021-08-20 08:12:49.000000', 0),
